# Surakkha — git line-ending rules.
#
# Force LF for files where CRLF would break the toolchain:
#   - *.prisma — Prisma 5.20.0's wasm validator rejects CRLF.
#   - *.sql    — Postgres runs the migration as written; CRLF in
#                .psql scripts is harmless but LF is conventional.
#   - Dockerfile, *.dockerfile — multi-stage builds assume LF;
#                Windows CRLF in COPY heredocs has been known to break.
#   - *.sh, *.bash — shell scripts that may run in Linux containers.
#
# Default everything else to LF (so a Windows dev clone stays
# canonical) but allow text files to be checked out as CRLF if the
# developer's `core.autocrlf=true` says so. The `text` attribute is
# the default; `text eol=lf` overrides it.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Files where CRLF would break parsing or runtime behaviour.
*.prisma        text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Binary files.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
